      "summary": "The trace lookup and duplicate handling follow the requested identifiers, but appended traces remain mutable through the caller's Steps collection, so the in-memory store can change without another append.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Persistence/CaseStateStore.cs",
          "line": 318,
          "message": "Copy or freeze each trace and its Steps before storing it so callers cannot mutate an appended record through a retained list reference.",
          "confidence": 0.9,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "AppendTrace stores the caller-supplied InvestigationTrace in the trace list; Freeze wraps the outer list but does not copy the trace's Steps list.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller appends a trace whose Steps is a mutable List, then changes an element in that list. FindTrace on the same store returns the changed step even though no append occurred, violating the append-only guarantee; a reload returns the original persisted step instead."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
