      "summary": "The named build-and-gate job runs the .NET test suite, and the tests cover the listed lookup, persistence, duplicate, and absent-trace criteria. However, a caller can mutate an appended trace's steps through a shared collection, violating append-only behavior.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Persistence/CaseStateStore.cs",
          "line": 579,
          "message": "Freeze does not copy or protect each trace's Steps collection, allowing callers to mutate an appended trace through the original collection.",
          "confidence": 0.97,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "AppendTrace stores the supplied InvestigationTrace, and Freeze wraps only the outer Traces list. The trace's Steps collection remains shared with the caller.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller passes a trace whose Steps is backed by a mutable array, appends it, then changes an array element. FindTrace on the same store returns the changed step while the persisted file still contains the original, so the supposedly append-only record changes and reads disagree before and after reload."
          }
        }
      ]
